<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE, GASOLINES UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE, GASOLINES UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Thursday it will cut its retail prices diesel in the Netherlands by 1.4 cents per litre with effect from October 26.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. It added that gasoline prices would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Saturday the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations goes down to 1.536 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
